nswer-field-07694784-baf6-5e51-adb3-374eb4370b43"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-07694784-baf6-5e51-adb3-374eb4370b43" :answer-field/id #uuid "07694784-baf6-5e51-adb3-374eb4370b43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a92a268-16d1-5dcb-b306-a7326a1b05cd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0600bda-d3d0-5f58-bde8-97ea12f74605" "answer-a0542525-2af1-509e-b992-a07e3969645a" "answer-5a92a268-16d1-5dcb-b306-a7326a1b05cd" "answer-145f15b2-ba16-5a91-9bf3-2a5912c459bd" "answer-9d016922-947d-5384-a572-6e8536e06491"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0600bda-d3d0-5f58-bde8-97ea12f74605" :answer/id #uuid "f0600bda-d3d0-5f58-bde8-97ea12f74605" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0542525-2af1-509e-b992-a07e3969645a" :answer/id #uuid "a0542525-2af1-509e-b992-a07e3969645a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$560$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a92a268-16d1-5dcb-b306-a7326a1b05cd" :answer/id #uuid "5a92a268-16d1-5dcb-b306-a7326a1b05cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$600$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-145f15b2-ba16-5a91-9bf3-2a5912c459bd" :answer/id #uuid "145f15b2-ba16-5a91-9bf3-2a5912c459bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$680$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d016922-947d-5384-a572-6e8536e06491" :answer/id #uuid "9d016922-947d-5384-a572-6e8536e06491" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$700$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d5dd58d1-f976-5297-ad4f-4ae9b9a92e73" :question/id #uuid "d5dd58d1-f976-5297-ad4f-4ae9b9a92e73" :question/math-academy-id "q-60058" :question/problem "Marcus has two water tanks. Tank A has a capacity of $1\\,508$ liters. The ratio of the capacity of tank A to the capacity of tank B is $3:4.$ By rounding the capacity of tank A to the nearest hundred, approximate the capacity of tank B." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the capacity of tank A:\n\n$$\n1\\,508⟶1\\,500\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the capacity of tank A to the capacity of tank B is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the capacity of tank A and the denominator represents the capacity of tank B.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $1,500$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $500$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 500}{4\\times 500}=\\frac{1\\,500}{2\\,000}\n$$\n\nTherefore, tank B has a capacity of approximately $2\\,000$ liters." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a81b6d9-bc7b-59de-a9a3-471d888208ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a81b6d9-bc7b-59de-a9a3-471d888208ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a81b6d9-bc7b-59de-a9a3-471d888208ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bf487438-5640-5153-989c-e0f9e3e1543b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-759966ab-ba62-5527-8d0c-c8bdec663c3c" "answer-15e18391-8e4a-5963-a8a7-7e77752d16d0" "answer-bf487438-5640-5153-989c-e0f9e3e1543b" "answer-1a2b62cc-53a5-556b-9fd6-5c8100d197ac" "answer-ef82b44a-93fe-5f33-918c-b074e3c3f194"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-759966ab-ba62-5527-8d0c-c8bdec663c3c" :answer/id #uuid "759966ab-ba62-5527-8d0c-c8bdec663c3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,600$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15e18391-8e4a-5963-a8a7-7e77752d16d0" :answer/id #uuid "15e18391-8e4a-5963-a8a7-7e77752d16d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,800$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf487438-5640-5153-989c-e0f9e3e1543b" :answer/id #uuid "bf487438-5640-5153-989c-e0f9e3e1543b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\,000$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a2b62cc-53a5-556b-9fd6-5c8100d197ac" :answer/id #uuid "1a2b62cc-53a5-556b-9fd6-5c8100d197ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\,100$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef82b44a-93fe-5f33-918c-b074e3c3f194" :answer/id #uuid "ef82b44a-93fe-5f33-918c-b074e3c3f194" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\,400$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e3b2f10a-1224-55b9-ac80-e23ac5f6c46a" :question/id #uuid "e3b2f10a-1224-55b9-ac80-e23ac5f6c46a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93289" :question/problem "The following table shows Herbert's height and the length of his shadow, in centimeters. \n\n| Height | Shadow |\n| --- | --- |\n| $197$ | $162$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the height of the object to the length of its ​shadow is the same for different objects at the same moment of time. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the length of the shadow cast by Regina at the same time, if her height is $150$ centimeters." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round Herbert's height and the length of his shadow:\n\n- Height: $197⟶200$\n\n- Shadow: $162⟶160$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the height to the length of the ​shadow (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{200}{160}.\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the height and the denominator represents the length of the ​shadow.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{200÷10}{160÷10}=\\frac{20}{16}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20÷4}{16÷4}=\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a numerator of $150$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $30$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 30}{4\\times 30}=\\frac{150}{120}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the shadow cast by Regina is approximately $120$ centimeters." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-482050e1-adac-56eb-8be8-fef04face0ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-482050e1-adac-56eb-8be8-fef04face0ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "482050e1-adac-56eb-8be8-fef04face0ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f86a78e6-512b-528a-8dea-49a6bf20da7d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b53fa937-0828-5202-94f7-21ca566eeb41" "answer-f86a78e6-512b-528a-8dea-49a6bf20da7d" "answer-0c107044-05cb-5b72-a382-8e1526bcaf66" "answer-9525c376-32d7-5e67-afa0-fc1bb38c14b5" "answer-426954b7-8774-5772-9e32-fda24a883750"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b53fa937-0828-5202-94f7-21ca566eeb41" :answer/id #uuid "b53fa937-0828-5202-94f7-21ca566eeb41" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$110$ centimeters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f86a78e6-512b-528a-8dea-49a6bf20da7d" :answer/id #uuid "f86a78e6-512b-528a-8dea-49a6bf20da7d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$120$ centimeters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c107044-05cb-5b72-a382-8e1526bcaf66" :answer/id #uuid "0c107044-05cb-5b72-a382-8e1526bcaf66" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$130$ centimeters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9525c376-32d7-5e67-afa0-fc1bb38c14b5" :answer/id #uuid "9525c376-32d7-5e67-afa0-fc1bb38c14b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$140$ centimeters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-426954b7-8774-5772-9e32-fda24a883750" :answer/id #uuid "426954b7-8774-5772-9e32-fda24a883750" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$160$ centimeters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e57d984e-c871-52fc-b8d7-34ff3957d67c" :question/id #uuid "e57d984e-c871-52fc-b8d7-34ff3957d67c" :question/math-academy-id "q-60067" :question/problem "The number of roses and orchids in Margaret's garden is shown in the following table:\n\n| Roses | Orchids |\n| --- | --- |\n| $33$ | $18$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIn Serena's garden, there are approximately $30$ orchids. The ratio of the number of roses to the number of orchids is equal in both gardens. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of roses in Serena's garden." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the number of roses and orchids in Margaret's garden:\n\n- Roses: $33⟶30$\n\n- Orchids: $18⟶20$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of roses to the number of orchids (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{20}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of roses and the denominator represents the number of orchids.\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $10$ gives an equivalent fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30÷10}{20÷10}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $15$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 15}{2\\times 15}=\\frac{45}{30}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $45$ roses in Serena's garden." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2915fff9-a5b4-5d3f-b71d-57e7e6ac1978"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2915fff9-a5b4-5d3f-b71d-57e7e6ac1978" :answer-field/id #uuid "2915fff9-a5b4-5d3f-b71d-57e7e6ac1978" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-16838127-1238-5d1a-86d2-c65647053407" :answer-field/choices ["answer-28e2d922-05ab-5c87-9a89-308a6939325d" "answer-16838127-1238-5d1a-86d2-c65647053407" "answer-70bfdf23-c8f9-5e45-8fc4-8dcadc5bacc7" "answer-6f1d3fdf-f980-58fa-80aa-e838556de0e0" "answer-b9eef285-487b-5f19-85cc-02493471b540"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28e2d922-05ab-5c87-9a89-308a6939325d" :answer/id #uuid "28e2d922-05ab-5c87-9a89-308a6939325d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$40$ roses" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16838127-1238-5d1a-86d2-c65647053407" :answer/id #uuid "16838127-1238-5d1a-86d2-c65647053407" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$45$ roses" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70bfdf23-c8f9-5e45-8fc4-8dcadc5bacc7" :answer/id #uuid "70bfdf23-c8f9-5e45-8fc4-8dcadc5bacc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$50$ roses" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f1d3fdf-f980-58fa-80aa-e838556de0e0" :answer/id #uuid "6f1d3fdf-f980-58fa-80aa-e838556de0e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$55$ roses" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9eef285-487b-5f19-85cc-02493471b540" :answer/id #uuid "b9eef285-487b-5f19-85cc-02493471b540" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$60$ roses" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d2ff2ee0-f6fe-5976-b859-e0adc12b8590" :question/id #uuid "d2ff2ee0-f6fe-5976-b859-e0adc12b8590" :question/math-academy-id "q-60069" :question/problem "The number of dogs and cats in shelter A is shown in the following table:\n\n| Dogs | Cats |\n| --- | --- |\n| $51$ | $32$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIn shelter B there are approximately $20$ dogs. The ratio of the number of dogs to the number of cats in both shelters is the same. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of cats in shelter B." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the number of dogs and cats in shelter A:\n\n- Dogs: $51⟶50$\n\n- Cats: $32⟶30$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of dogs to the number of cats (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{50}{30}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of dogs and the denominator represents the number of cats.\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $10$ gives an equivalent fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{50÷10}{30÷10}=\\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nWe can make a numerator of $20$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 4}{3\\times 4}=\\frac{20}{12}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $12$ cats in shelter B." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3dbb387d-7a25-5bb2-8ab3-ac3326b883b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3dbb387d-7a25-5bb2-8ab3-ac3326b883b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "3dbb387d-7a25-5bb2-8ab3-ac3326b883b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d1645bab-1cbe-5d0a-a07e-c8d791cb10d1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d6112a9b-d3bc-512d-aa34-95b96d7cf8ff" "answer-d1645bab-1cbe-5d0a-a07e-c8d791cb10d1" "answer-eb3b4d3f-4f3a-56fd-b4da-2c25a2897600" "answer-2c00f90c-1fb9-5090-9bb2-9a477735cada" "answer-1acabbdc-ca40-5169-86fa-94633dbacba8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6112a9b-d3bc-512d-aa34-95b96d7cf8ff" :answer/id #uuid "d6112a9b-d3bc-512d-aa34-95b96d7cf8ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10$ cats" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1645bab-1cbe-5d0a-a07e-c8d791cb10d1" :answer/id #uuid "d1645bab-1cbe-5d0a-a07e-c8d791cb10d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ cats" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb3b4d3f-4f3a-56fd-b4da-2c25a2897600" :answer/id #uuid "eb3b4d3f-4f3a-56fd-b4da-2c25a2897600" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$14$ cats" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c00f90c-1fb9-5090-9bb2-9a477735cada" :answer/id #uuid "2c00f90c-1fb9-5090-9bb2-9a477735cada" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16$ cats" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1acabbdc-ca40-5169-86fa-94633dbacba8" :answer/id #uuid "1acabbdc-ca40-5169-86fa-94633dbacba8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$18$ cats" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5ec248fa-4181-5322-854b-62b56bba8e0b" :question/id #uuid "5ec248fa-4181-5322-854b-62b56bba8e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60072" :question/problem "The following table shows the number of babies born at a hospital in New York during a particular month:\n\n| Boys | Girls |\n| --- | --- |\n| $102$ | $81$ |\n\nApproximately $120$ girls were born at a hospital in Boston during the same month. The ratio of boys to girls was the same at both hospitals. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of boys born at the Boston hospital during that month." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the number of babies born in the New York Hospital to the nearest $10$:\n\n- Boys: $102⟶100$\n\n- Girls: $81⟶80$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{100}{80}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of boys and the denominator represents the number of girls.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{100÷10}{80÷10}=\\frac{10}{8}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10÷2}{8÷2}=\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $120$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $30$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 30}{4\\times 30}=\\frac{150}{120}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $150$ boys were born at Boston Hospital in that particular month." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1a7abed6-6b73-5db6-ab00-05e20862640c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1a7abed6-6b73-5db6-ab00-05e20862640c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a7abed6-6b73-5db6-ab00-05e20862640c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b7e8fb97-82f3-5cac-8b36-f2c0be1282ae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-66b5e765-8394-5e26-97cb-5181ad7de253" "answer-fc0b57ff-09b4-5306-9f7f-2157afda7e05" "answer-b7e8fb97-82f3-5cac-8b36-f2c0be1282ae" "answer-dfa9376f-970b-5851-b63a-06d19f7a9bda" "answer-8267c91e-78e7-54f1-810d-56e688dacbb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66b5e765-8394-5e26-97cb-5181ad7de253" :answer/id #uuid "66b5e765-8394-5e26-97cb-5181ad7de253" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$125$ boys" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc0b57ff-09b4-5306-9f7f-2157afda7e05" :answer/id #uuid "fc0b57ff-09b4-5306-9f7f-2157afda7e05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$130$ boys" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7e8fb97-82f3-5cac-8b36-f2c0be1282ae" :answer/id #uuid "b7e8fb97-82f3-5cac-8b36-f2c0be1282ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$150$ boys" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfa9376f-970b-5851-b63a-06d19f7a9bda" :answer/id #uuid "dfa9376f-970b-5851-b63a-06d19f7a9bda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$160$ boys" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8267c91e-78e7-54f1-810d-56e688dacbb9" :answer/id #uuid "8267c91e-78e7-54f1-810d-56e688dacbb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$180$ boys" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b402cb00-d472-5e9f-9484-7067afb16406" :question/id #uuid "b402cb00-d472-5e9f-9484-7067afb16406" :question/math-academy-id "q-93275" :question/problem "The building model has the same ratio of length to width as a real building\nThe following table shows the length and width of the building model in centimeters. \n\n| Length | Width |\n| --- | --- |\n| $84$ | $41$ |\n\nBy rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the length of the building if it is known that its width is $20$ meters." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the length and width of the building model:\n\n- Length: $84⟶80$\n\n- Width: $41⟶40$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the length to the width (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{80}{40}.\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the length of the building model, and the denominator represents the width.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{80÷10}{40÷10}=\\frac{8}{4}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8÷4}{4÷4}=\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $20$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $20$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 20}{1\\times 20}=\\frac{40}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the building is approximately $40$ meters." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d9b0300d-ca77-5e40-9b4f-6ccf069cb4cb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d9b0300d-ca77-5e40-9b4f-6ccf069cb4cb" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9b0300d-ca77-5e40-9b4f-6ccf069cb4cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ee1aba69-437e-53d8-939e-e999b50e2e01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf27713d-59bd-56e8-bb75-d1acd34b7f7e" "answer-ee1aba69-437e-53d8-939e-e999b50e2e01" "answer-28615b6e-6fc5-5804-9afc-6daf868b4ac8" "answer-553bf0cf-1717-5c73-8656-42c8cfbe753c" "answer-01f8dab9-a608-5cd8-9379-13466349cb11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf27713d-59bd-56e8-bb75-d1acd34b7f7e" :answer/id #uuid "bf27713d-59bd-56e8-bb75-d1acd34b7f7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$35$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee1aba69-437e-53d8-939e-e999b50e2e01" :answer/id #uuid "ee1aba69-437e-53d8-939e-e999b50e2e01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$40$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28615b6e-6fc5-5804-9afc-6daf868b4ac8" :answer/id #uuid "28615b6e-6fc5-5804-9afc-6daf868b4ac8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$48$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-553bf0cf-1717-5c73-8656-42c8cfbe753c" :answer/id #uuid "553bf0cf-1717-5c73-8656-42c8cfbe753c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$50$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01f8dab9-a608-5cd8-9379-13466349cb11" :answer/id #uuid "01f8dab9-a608-5cd8-9379-13466349cb11" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$52$ meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "tutorial-777fe794-e3cc-5250-a9e8-e407cc3f306c" :tutorial/id #uuid "777fe794-e3cc-5250-a9e8-e407cc3f306c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2052 :tutorial/title "Introduction" :tutorial/content "We can use what we know about rounding numbers to approximate ratios.\nWe round the quantities to a given degree first, before setting up the ratio.\n\nLook at the following table, which shows the number of girls in a ballet school with blonde or black hair.\n\n| Blonde Hair | Black Hair |\n| --- | --- |\n| $33$ | $58$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest ten, let's determine the approximate ratio of girls with blonde hair to girls with black hair.\n\nFirst, let's approximate the number of girls with blonde or black hair by rounding to the nearest ten.\n\n- Number of girls with blonde hair: $33 \\longrightarrow 30$\n\n- Number of girls with black hair: $58 \\longrightarrow 60$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of girls with blonde hair to the number of girls with black hair is approximately\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{30}{60}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{30 \\div 10}{60 \\div 10} = \\dfrac{3}{6}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3 \\div 3}{6 \\div 3} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of girls with blonde hair to the number of girls with black hair is approximately $\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id "tutorial-16e103a1-de00-5acb-9566-24168dec17eb" :tutorial/id #uuid "16e103a1-de00-5acb-9566-24168dec17eb" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14923 :tutorial/title "Finding a Value Given a Ratio" :tutorial/content "Now, let's see how we can find a value given the ratio and another value.\n\nSuppose at a school library, there are some science books and $396$ history books. The ratio of the number of science books to the number of history books is $3: 4.$ By rounding the number of history books to the nearest ten, approximate the number of science books in the library.\n\nFirst, let's approximate the number of history books:\n\n$$\n396 \\longrightarrow 400\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the number of science books to the number of history books is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{\\color{red}4}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nHere, \n\n- the numerator represents the number of science books, and\n\n- the denominator represents the number of history books.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $400$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $100{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3 \\times 100}{4 \\times 100} = \\dfrac{300}{400}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $300$ science books in the library." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id "activity-37d9328b-f5cc-5af8-87e2-f52cd07d5248" :activity/id #uuid "37d9328b-f5cc-5af8-87e2-f52cd07d5248" :activity/title "Approximating Ratios" :activity/type :activity.type/lesson :activity/scope 17592186048840 :activity/expected-seconds 1200.0 :activity/steps ["step-805b138d-9de3-5c18-96bd-507752cfcb3d" "step-aa6626df-e1ca-57ff-8e3c-685699ee9c0c" "step-64bb8dc3-c0c9-5342-9899-e92b00265817" "step-9d54fdb2-7a7b-5fda-81dd-61e03fb3fa56" "step-3990eff7-9439-5ea7-a839-81c63a117a93" "step-39d2b0a2-a796-5c2d-87be-ef9b250b51be"] :activity/first-step "step-805b138d-9de3-5c18-96bd-507752cfcb3d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-805b138d-9de3-5c18-96bd-507752cfcb3d" :step/id #uuid "805b138d-9de3-5c18-96bd-507752cfcb3d" :step/content "tutorial-777fe794-e3cc-5250-a9e8-e407cc3f306c" :step/math-academy-id 648000 :step/next "step-aa6626df-e1ca-57ff-8e3c-685699ee9c0c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-aa6626df-e1ca-57ff-8e3c-685699ee9c0c" :step/id #uuid "aa6626df-e1ca-57ff-8e3c-685699ee9c0c" :step/content "knowledge-point-10523576-ab54-5731-bfaf-999a591295e0" :step/math-academy-id 648001 :step/next "step-64bb8dc3-c0c9-5342-9899-e92b00265817" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-64bb8dc3-c0c9-5342-9899-e92b00265817" :step/id #uuid "64bb8dc3-c0c9-5342-9899-e92b00265817" :step/content "knowledge-point-c71ff81f-388d-53c8-853e-c60430327148" :step/math-academy-id 648005 :step/next "step-9d54fdb2-7a7b-5fda-81dd-61e03fb3fa56" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9d54fdb2-7a7b-5fda-81dd-61e03fb3fa56" :step/id #uuid "9d54fdb2-7a7b-5fda-81dd-61e03fb3fa56" :step/content "tutorial-16e103a1-de00-5acb-9566-24168dec17eb" :step/math-academy-id 648008 :step/next "step-3990eff7-9439-5ea7-a839-81c63a117a93" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3990eff7-9439-5ea7-a839-81c63a117a93" :step/id #uuid "3990eff7-9439-5ea7-a839-81c63a117a93" :step/content "knowledge-point-01f99115-f376-50c2-9b7e-79800006d437" :step/math-academy-id 648009 :step/next "step-39d2b0a2-a796-5c2d-87be-ef9b250b51be" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-39d2b0a2-a796-5c2d-87be-ef9b250b51be" :step/id #uuid "39d2b0a2-a796-5c2d-87be-ef9b250b51be" :step/content "knowledge-point-a02676df-7c77-5303-9d8e-7c83fdfd2060" :step/math-academy-id 648012 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
